<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19989" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Grȳnīa</span></b> , ae,
			f., and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Grȳnĭum</span></b>  (also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Grūnium</span></b>  in some editt. of Nep.),
			ii, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γρύνεια</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γρύνιον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a small town in
				Æolis</i>, <i>with a temple of
			Apollo</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 30, 32, § 121</span></i>; <i><span class="en">32, 6, 21, §
			59</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Nep. Alc. 9, 3</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Deriv. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Grȳnēus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γρύνειος</span>, <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Grynia</i>, <i>Grynian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Apollo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 4, 345</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nemus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. E.
					6, 72</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
